==Strategy==
For Chapters 1 & 2, bringing [[:Category:Cats with Warp Immunity|Cats with Warp Immunity]] is key to a strong defence against Project A due to his quick attacks, while cheap attackers such as [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] to clear the peons. Bring [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] attackers and ranged units to deal with him from afar. For Chapter 3, bring [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] as well, to stall Cyberhorn.

For Chapter 1 cheese, bring a Lv.30 [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and a meatshield (preferrably crazed ones). The rest of the lineup is for combos or ubers for a faster win. Start by saving. Don't upgrade the worker cat. Once the first Croco is about 1/4 to the base, send out a crazed meatshield, and briefly after, followed by a courier. The point here is for the meatshield to reach and stall the croco first so that it doesn't move into the blindspot of courier. Once the first few crocos and kroxos (if not mistaken 4 in total) are taken care of by the courier, send out Bahamut. Bahamut should be able to hit Project A directly and the latter should die in two hits by Bahamut. (Two hits with the first two treasure sets in COTC in 100%) After sending out Bahamut, you may send whatever that's left and win.

